.TH MW-SERVE 1 "2026-09-06" "MemoryWhale 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-serve \- local dashboard, HTTP MCP, and opt-in read-only JSON API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-serve
.RI [ --lan ]
.RI [ --host
.IR addr ]
.RI [ --port
.IR n ]
.RI [ --token
.IR secret ]
.RI [ --print-token ]
.RI [ --api ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-serve
runs a small, dependency-free HTTP server that renders the local MemoryWhale
database as a browsable dashboard: recorded sessions, command runs with their
full command lines, projects grouped by working directory, and an interactive
knowledge graph. It reads the same local SQLite database written by
.BR mw (1)
and
.BR mw-remember (1)
and serves entirely from the local machine.
.PP
On start it self-heals by importing any session transcripts whose recording was
interrupted before its database row was written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--host " addr
Address to bind. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B --lan
Bind to
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
LAN access requires a token:
.B MEMORYWHALE_TOKEN ,
.BR --token ,
or a minted
.B serve.token
file.
.TP
.BI "--port " n
TCP port to listen on. Default
.BR 7071 .
.TP
.BI "--token " secret
Require a shared token, including on loopback. Overrides
.BR MEMORYWHALE_TOKEN .
Protected HTTP MCP requests must use Bearer authentication; JSON API requests
may use Bearer authentication or the dashboard login cookie.
.TP
.B --api
Enable the read-only
.B /api/v1
JSON API (disabled by default). Includes health, search, memory-by-ID,
command-by-ID, session-list, and repository/worktree endpoints. Search and
list responses are capped at 50 items. There are no API write, arbitrary SQL,
or arbitrary file-read endpoints. The API shares the dashboard's listener,
request bounds, host checks, and token gate.
.TP
.B --print-token
Print the token this process would use and exit without binding.
This can mint
.B serve.token
even without
.BR --lan .
Default loopback serving stays open unless
.B --token
or
.B MEMORYWHALE_TOKEN
is set.
.SH HTTP MCP
.B POST /mcp
on the same port is one JSON-RPC object per request (no SSE session).
Clients may send
.B 2026-07-28
.B _meta
on each request, or a legacy
.B initialize
handshake then
.BR tools/list .
Loopback is open by default. An explicit
.B --token
or a LAN bind requires
.B Authorization: Bearer
matching the dashboard token.
.PP
The same six tools as
.BR mw-mcp (1)
are available independently of
.BR --api .
MCP can explicitly write a lesson through
.BR remember ;
agent-authored lessons are pending review by default. MCP access alone does
not capture terminal commands.
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.nf
GET /api/v1/health
GET /api/v1/search?q=text&limit=20&agent=claude
GET /api/v1/memories/:id
GET /api/v1/commands/:id
GET /api/v1/sessions?limit=20
GET /api/v1/repositories
.fi
.PP
The optional search agent filter accepts claude, rho, or terminal. Terminal
matches NULL provenance, including manual and legacy records. Agent is
separate from the command/session/note source type. Memory IDs are namespaced;
command IDs are raw command_runs IDs, exposed as command_id in search results.
.SH SECURITY
Default loopback serving is open unless a token is explicitly configured.
Non-loopback serving requires a token and should be limited to trusted
networks. HTTP does not encrypt the token or retrieved evidence.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR
Select the local memory store and persistent serve.token directory.
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_TOKEN
Set an explicit access token without a command-line argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Localhost only:
.B mw-serve
.TP
Local dashboard, HTTP MCP, and read-only JSON API:
.B mw-serve --api
.TP
Authenticated LAN access at port 8080:
.B MEMORYWHALE_TOKEN=shared-secret mw-serve --lan --port 8080
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-remember (1),
.BR mw-mcp (1)
